From bd2b012a466bb54c2da02f925b1ceb49252f8742 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:11:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] Take over a pane's running shell after a page reload

The page asks the PTY server for its pane's shell (`pane=` on the new-session URL). When the
server still has that shell running, it replies with `adopt` (the shell's Warp session ids and
whether a command runs) and replays the shell's bootstrap plus its output since the latest
prompt. Warp then skips writing the env and bootstrap script, registers the session ids so the
replayed hooks are accepted, drops terminal replies during the replay and, while a command runs,
its own input for a moment afterwards, so nothing stray reaches the running program.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
